    "methodology": "A record is included only when a source feature is an exact official roster name after harmless punctuation/case normalization, or a recorded explicit alias. Generic railway points with a name collision were excluded unless the source name or an official line-qualified name makes metro identity unambiguous. Point coordinates are unchanged; station-footprint polygons are represented by their calculated centroids and retain the polygon source ID. No coordinates were interpolated from line geometry.",
    "limitations": [
      "This is a partial supplement, not a complete Mumbai Metro dataset. It now includes all 12 Line 1 stations using OSM points or station-footprint centroids, 17 of 27 Line 3 stations, five of six currently open Line 2B stations, and all four currently open Line 9 stations. Missing points remain missing; no station is placed from a schematic.",
      "The Line 3 Aarey source point is already present in public/data/metro-stations-osm.json as a Line 7 record, so it is not duplicated here even though the physical area is also served by Line 3.",
      "Ambiguous generic suburban-rail records such as Churchgate, Mumbai Central, Grant Road, and Dadar were not included. A name match alone does not prove that an unqualified source point represents the underground Line 3 station.",
      "Station rosters validate names and corridor membership; the HOTOSM export itself does not reliably carry metro operator or line tags. Kochi's Vyttila and Pune's Mahatma Phule Mandai are included from source objects that were absent from the first curated point bundle."
    ],
    "validation": {
      "sourceCoordinateEquality": "Point features retain source coordinates; centroid features retain their source polygon IDs and are reproducible from its closed ring in data/source/hotosm/railways.geojson.",
      "duplicateFeatureIds": "Checked against this file and public/data/metro-stations-osm.json; no duplicate source feature IDs are included."
    }
  },
